# Amendment #25 — memory-system BGE reranker swap

`make_graphiti` now passes an explicit `cross_encoder=
LazyBGERerankerClient()` to the `Graphiti` constructor.
Eliminates a latent missing-`OPENAI_API_KEY` failure in the
rerank path: graphiti-core 0.28.2 silently defaults unset
`cross_encoder` to `OpenAIRerankerClient()`, whose first
`rank()` call raises `openai.AuthenticationError` because we
never configure `OPENAI_API_KEY` (amendment #8 removed billed-
API coupling from the LLM path; the reranker was the last
holdout).

The local replacement is `graphiti_core.cross_encoder.
bge_reranker_client.BGERerankerClient`, backed by the
`BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3` cross-encoder via
`sentence-transformers` (new dep, `>=3.2.1` floor matching
graphiti-core's declared extra).

Lazy wrapper (`LazyBGERerankerClient`) defers the BGE model
load from `__init__` to first `rank()` call. Without it,
factory construction would trigger a ~1 GB HF download on
first run and seconds of weight load even when warm —
unacceptable for the pytest suite and for amendment #24's MCP
service startup (which calls `make_graphiti` at every launchd
KeepAlive restart). With it, only `graphiti.search()` calls
that actually exercise reranking pay the one-time load cost.

No behaviour change on paths that don't invoke reranking.
Shape-only assertion landed in
`memory-system/tests/test_factory.py::test_AC25_1_*`.

# Amendment #30 — memory-system env-scrubber USER widening + pre-spawn structural check

2026-04-24. Closes the USER-missing defect that shipped through
the amendment #8 and amendment #11 seals: macOS launchd's
gui-domain session injects USER into spawned agent processes,
but memory-system's `_ENV_ALLOWED_VARS` tuple only admitted
PATH and HOME — so the scrubber silently dropped USER from the
child env for every `claude -p` subprocess. Without USER,
`claude`'s OAuth keychain lookup fails and the CLI emits "Not
logged in · Please run /login" even on an authenticated host.

Re-extension of amendment #8's AC2 per ODD §4. No new error-code
block; the amendment widens one presence-side invariant of the
existing scrubbed-env contract.

Structural remedy (research §Q3; §Q1 empirical bisection):

  - `_ENV_ALLOWED_VARS` gains `"USER"`. Every other candidate
    surveyed in research §Q3 (LOGNAME, __CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING,
    TMPDIR, SHELL, LANG, and the forbidden API-key vars) is
    ruled OUT with evidence and must stay OUT under the §2.5
    code-for-cases-no-objective-names discipline. HOME retains
    membership — load-bearing for future ~/.claude/* config
    reads per research §Q3 row 2.
  - The AC2 test extends with a positive-presence clause: under
    a parent env monkeypatched to carry USER=<controlled-value>,
    the constructed child-env dict carries USER bound to the
    same value. Forbidden-key absence and PATH-presence
    assertions preserved verbatim.
  - A new pre-spawn structural-inspection test captures the
    child-env dict that would be passed to
    `asyncio.create_subprocess_exec` and asserts USER is present
    and equal to the login user's value. The subprocess is
    never actually executed — the invariant is on the scrubber's
    output, not a behavioural observation of a real claude
    process. Future regression surfaces as a failing
    deterministic test on a dict invariant, not as a runtime
    "Not logged in" error in production.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Test-shape: research §Q2 candidate (A) — construction-time
    assertion on the scrubbed-env dict's contents via the same
    `asyncio.create_subprocess_exec` mock AC2 already uses.
    Candidate (B) real-`claude` subprocess and candidate (C)
    fake-claude binary are explicitly out-of-scope per owner
    ruling 2026-04-24.
  - Parent-env seeding: `monkeypatch.setenv("USER",
    "<controlled-value>")` in both AC tests. Fail-closed
    direction preserved: when the parent env lacks USER at
    construction time, the scrubbed dict simply omits it — no
    synthesis, no fallback value.

Fail-closed behaviours preserved:

  - ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / OPENAI_API_KEY / GEMINI_API_KEY remain
    forbidden from the child env (AC2 absence invariants).
  - PATH remains in the child env with the hardcoded fallback
    when the parent env lacks PATH (AC2 positive invariant).
  - --bare never appears in argv (AC2 argv-shape invariant).

AC surface (AC-i, AC-ii):

  - AC-i: the AC2 test file extends with a positive-assertion
    clause: under a monkeypatched parent env, child env carries
    USER=<controlled-value>.
  - AC-ii: a new pre-spawn structural-inspection test on the
    constructed `_child_env` dict asserts USER presence +
    equality with the login-user value set via monkeypatch.

Out of scope (per amendment plan §6):

  - LOGNAME, TMPDIR, SHELL, LANG, __CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING, and
    every other candidate surveyed in research §Q3 — each ruled
    OUT with evidence.
  - Real-claude-binary test fixtures (research §Q2 candidate B).
  - Fake-claude subprocess fixtures (research §Q2 candidate C).
  - Any cross-component generalisation of the "scrubbed-env
    subprocess" harness pattern (research §Q4; FUTURE_IDEAS).
  - POST_FIRST_RUN_REVIEW.md register updates (research §Q4 —
    may be carried separately).
  - Any change to launchd plist, adapter wiring, or MCP
    transport surface.

BASELINE a010686 (pre-amendment tip). memory-system's
SEAL_COMMIT sidecar lands at a010686 on the amendment commit
for the empty-diff window; advanced to the amendment SHA in
the seal commit via `pos-amend seal`. H19 cross-cutting seal
test is NOT touched — no manifest entry, no sidecar bump.
